{"step_index":2761,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T16:41:01Z","thinking":"**Investigating the Connection Error**\n\nI'm currently looking into why I got the \"Unable to reach the Surge API\" message. The core of the problem seems to stem from `surge.loginForm` making a request to `request.join(config.endpoint, 'token')`. This endpoint points to `api.surge.io` or `surge.surge.sh` over HTTP port 80.  The DNS lookup returned `138.197.235.123` for these, so that is the starting point.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"const dns = require('dns');\\nconst origLookup = dns.lookup;\\ndns.lookup = function(hostname, options, callback) {\\n  if (typeof options === 'function') {\\n    callback = options;\\n    options = {};\\n  }\\n  if (hostname === 'surge.surge.sh' || hostname === 'surge.sh' || hostname === 'valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh') {\\n    return callback(null, '138.197.235.123', 4);\\n  }\\n  return origLookup(hostname, options, callback);\\n};\\n\\n// Execute surge CLI with https endpoint\\nconst surge = require('C:/Users/brorm/AppData/Local/npm-cache/_npx/23158936acd5c32d/node_modules/surge')({\\n  endpoint: 'https://surge.surge.sh'\\n});\\nsurge(['./dist', 'valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh', '--endpoint', 'https://surge.surge.sh']);\\n\"","Description":"\"Update deploy-surge.js to enforce https endpoint\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\brorm\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\snap-dialer\\\\deploy-surge.js\"","toolAction":"\"Updating deploy-surge.js for https\"","toolSummary":"\"Update deploy-surge.js for https\""}}]}
